From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Vishnefske <jvishnefske@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 18:27:19 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] std: fixes found by std's unit tests on linux-none

Building std as a member of the library workspace, as x.py does (and
as std's unit tests need), turns on std's own lints, which
-Zbuild-std caps. Running the tests then found two real differences
from std on linux-gnu.

- Lints: pointers passed to ioctl/prctl went through `as usize`,
  which std denies (implicit_provenance_casts); expose their
  provenance instead, and make JoinHandleExt's pthread_t with
  with_exposed_provenance_mut. Silence the warnings that only
  linux-none's cfgs cause: the unused `fds` initializer in pipe(),
  the unsafe block around close (a safe call here) in OwnedFd::drop,
  and pal::unsupported{,_err}, which nothing on linux-none uses.
- Cargo.lock: record linux_none_rt and the patched libc, so cargo
  stops rewriting the lock file of the patched tree.
- errno moves to linux_none_rt::errno. It was a thread-local in std,
  so each copy of std in a program had its own: std's unit tests link
  the std under test and the sysroot's, whose io::Error methods (such
  as last_os_error) read the other copy's errno and saw 0 for every
  failed socket call. libc's errno is shared the same way.
- ExitStatus's Display names the signal ("signal: 15 (SIGTERM)"), as
  std's unix code does on Linux; linux-none printed only the number.
---
 library/Cargo.lock                            | 10 +++-
 library/std/src/os/fd/owned.rs                |  2 +
 library/std/src/sys/fd/linux_none.rs          |  3 +-
 library/std/src/sys/io/error/linux_none.rs    | 10 ++--
 .../std/src/sys/io/is_terminal/linux_none.rs  |  3 +-
 library/std/src/sys/pal/linux_none/mod.rs     |  2 +
 library/std/src/sys/pipe/unix.rs              |  3 +-
 .../std/src/sys/process/unix/linux_none.rs    | 50 +++++++++++++++++--
 library/std/src/sys/thread/linux_none.rs      |  4 +-
 9 files changed, 70 insertions(+), 17 deletions(-)

